\@writefile{tdo}{\contentsline {todo}{\fcolorbox {black}{orange}{\textcolor {orange}{o}}\  Get back to this and illustrate: \par One crucial observation here is that SHAP explains predictions, not outcomes. If $f(x) = \mathbb  {E}[Y \mid X=x]$ (as in regression), then SHAP explains $\mathbb  {E}[Y \mid X=x] - \mathbb  {E}[Y]$. The residual $Y - f(x)$ --- the noise --- is entirely invisible to SHAP by construction. }{19}{section*.10}\protected@file@percent }
